# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the value. `.env` is gitignored.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Get a free Web3Forms access key at https://web3forms.com - you enter the email
# address you want enquiries sent to, and they email you the key.
#
# The PUBLIC_ prefix is deliberate: Astro only exposes prefixed variables to the
# built output, and this key genuinely does need to reach the browser (it sits in
# a hidden field in the contact form). It is not a secret. It is kept out of the
# repo so that copies of this template do not all point at the same inbox.
#
# Set the same variable in your host's dashboard when you deploy:
#   Cloudflare Pages - Settings > Environment variables
#   Netlify          - Site settings > Environment variables
#
# Leave it unset and the contact form renders disabled with a visible warning,
# rather than silently dropping enquiries.
PUBLIC_WEB3FORMS_KEY=
